            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex pattern to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nThe regex works as follows:\n\n- **Line validation**: `^(?=...IPv4...)` - Anchors to the line start and lookahead-checks for a valid IPv4 address anywhere on the line\n- **Greedy matching**: `.*` - Matches everything up to the last potential date\n- **Date boundary check**: `(?<![A-Za-z0-9])` and `(?![A-Za-z0-9])` - Ensures no alphanumeric characters immediately before/after the date\n- **Proper date validation**: Separate patterns for 31-day, 30-day, and February dates\n- **Last-date guarantee**: `[^0-9-]*$` - Ensures no digits or dashes follow the matched date (which would indicate another date), only trailing non-numeric content\n\nThe regex will correctly reject false matches like `user1134-12-1234` while accepting valid dates like `2026-02-29`, and will capture only the last date when multiple dates appear on the same line with an IPv4 address."
